# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore for parent-context builds rooted at vibemind-os/
# =============================================================================
# The Brain image (brain/the_brain/Dockerfile) builds with context=vibemind-os/
# so it can reach the local `shared/` package. Without this file the context
# would include coding-engine (~913M), spaces, voice, openfang, etc. — making
# every build pull >1.5GB. Whitelist ONLY what the Brain build needs.
#
# .dockerignore is relative to the build context root, so this file (at
# vibemind-os/) supersedes brain/the_brain/.dockerignore for these builds.
# =============================================================================

# Exclude everything by default …
*

# … then re-include only the two trees the Brain image needs.
!brain/
!shared/

# Build artefacts / caches inside the re-included trees (these patterns are
# matched at any depth, so they prune the kept subtrees too).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.git/
**/.github/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Secrets never go into an image layer (provided at runtime via env_file).
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.bak

# Brain runtime logs (the persistent ./data volume is mounted at run time;
# logs would just bloat the context).
brain/the_brain/data/logs/
brain/the_brain/logs/

# Bulky non-essential
**/*.zip
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
